Default logind-handle-lid-switch to TRUE

Tenko owns lid policy in systemd-logind (see the 10-lid-switch.conf drop-in
from tenko-sysconfig), so the power manager must not claim handle-lid-switch
with a block inhibitor.  Claiming it makes logind stand down before it looks
at the configured HandleLidSwitch action, which leaves the lid doing nothing
outside XFCE's own settings.  With this default XFCE sessions inherit the
same desktop-independent suspend policy as any other session.

The setting stays overridable per user with

  xfconf-query -c xfce4-power-manager \
    -p /xfce4-power-manager/logind-handle-lid-switch -n -t bool -s false

--- a/common/xfpm-config.h
+++ b/common/xfpm-config.h
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
 #define LOGIND_HANDLE_HIBERNATE_KEY "logind-handle-hibernate-key"
 #define DEFAULT_LOGIND_HANDLE_HIBERNATE_KEY FALSE
 #define LOGIND_HANDLE_LID_SWITCH "logind-handle-lid-switch"
-#define DEFAULT_LOGIND_HANDLE_LID_SWITCH FALSE
+#define DEFAULT_LOGIND_HANDLE_LID_SWITCH TRUE
 
 #define BRIGHTNESS_ON_AC "brightness-on-ac"
 #define MIN_BRIGHTNESS_ON_AC 9
